  "summary": "Beaver County, Pennsylvania's behavioral health department was hit by a ransomware attack in August 2025 when a foreign hacker group encrypted patient records and blocked employee access to systems managing mental health, intellectual disability, early intervention, and substance abuse services. The attackers stole sensitive medical information and threatened to publish records unless the county paid a ransom. County Solicitor Garen Fedeles publicly confirmed the incident on Aug. 5, and commissioners paid $175,000 in cryptocurrency using opioid-settlement funds to regain access. The county has not disclosed entry method, whether a working decryptor was provided, the full scope of stolen data, or affected individual count.",
